{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/torvalds/linux/compare/master...5258572aa5fd5a7ed01b123b28241e0281b6fb9b","html_url":"https://github.com/torvalds/linux/compare/master...5258572aa5fd5a7ed01b123b28241e0281b6fb9b","permalink_url":"https://github.com/torvalds/linux/compare/torvalds:f802b65...torvalds:5258572","diff_url":"https://github.com/torvalds/linux/compare/master...5258572aa5fd5a7ed01b123b28241e0281b6fb9b.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/torvalds/linux/compare/master...5258572aa5fd5a7ed01b123b28241e0281b6fb9b.patch","base_commit":{"sha":"f802b6558eb81bd5888d761a0cdc8afe5fd8c941","node_id":"C_kwDOACN7MtoAKGY4MDJiNjU1OGViODFiZDU4ODhkNzYxYTBjZGM4YWZlNWZkOGM5NDE","commit":{"author":{"name":"Linus Torvalds","email":"torvalds@linux-foundation.org","date":"2026-11-21T23:36:04Z"},"committer":{"name":"Linus Torvalds","email":"torvalds@linux-foundation.org","date":"2026-11-21T23:36:04Z"},"message":"Merge tag 'xfs-fixes-7.4-rc4' of git://git.kernel.org:/pub/scm/fs/xfs/xfs-linux\n\nPull xfs fixes from Carlos Maiolino:\n \"Mostly this includes fixes for a few races, an ordering problem during\n  init/teardown of proc/sysfs, missing locks, etc\"\n\n* tag 'xfs-fixes-7.4-rc4' of git://git.kernel.org:/pub/scm/fs/xfs/xfs-linux:\n  xfs: test for realtime and reflink under the pNFS locks\n  xfs: don't enable DAX on zoned inodes\n  xfs: restart faults racing with realtime flag changes\n  xfs: take the MMAPLOCK in xfs_fileattr_set()\n  xfs: refuse fallocate racing with realtime flag changes\n  xfs: test for always COW after the dio write checks\n  xfs: refuse writes to files racing with realtime inode flag changes\n  xfs: test for reflink after the dio write checks\n  xfs: properly order xfsstats proc/sysfs init and teardown\n  xfs: remove unused variable in xrep_tempfile_copyin()\n  xfs: remove unused variable in xchk_stats_estimate_bufsize()\n  xfs: fix f_bfree underflow in statfs()\n  xfs: wait for direct I/O before swapping extents\n  xfs: break layouts before swapping extents\n  iomap: don't punch delalloc under a dirty EOF block\n  xfs: don't change the block map under a dirty folio\n  xfs: flush the shifted range before changing the file\n  xfs: don't skip the flush before shifting extents\n  xfs: always call xfs_update_stable_writes in xfs_ioctl_setattr_xflags\n  xfs: keep successful near rt allocations","tree":{"sha":"15dca1b3e51cc361db1e1376f3f9c4cebefaf747","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/torvalds/linux/git/trees/15dca1b3e51cc361db1e1376f3f9c4cebefaf747"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/torvalds/linux/git/commits/f802b6558eb81bd5888d761a0cdc8afe5fd8c941","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":false,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"payload":null,"verified_at":null}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/torvalds/linux/commits/f802b6558eb81bd5888d761a0cdc8afe5fd8c941","html_url":"https://github.com/torvalds/linux/commit/f802b6558eb81bd5888d761a0cdc8afe5fd8c941","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/torvalds/linux/commits/f802b6558eb81bd5888d761a0cdc8afe5fd8c941/comments","author":{"login":"torvalds","id":1024025,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEwMjQwMjU=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1024025?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/torvalds","html_url":"https://github.com/torvalds","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/torvalds/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/torvalds/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/torvalds/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/torvalds/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/torvalds/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/torvalds/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/torvalds/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/torvalds/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/torvalds/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"torvalds","id":1024025,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEwMjQwMjU=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1024025?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/torvalds","html_url":"https://github.com/torvalds","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/torvalds/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/torvalds/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/torvalds/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/torvalds/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/torvalds/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/torvalds/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/torvalds/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/torvalds/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/torvalds/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"62b13f41be6284250c06ab4d79a7fb13fe93f4d7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/torvalds/linux/commits/62b13f41be6284250c06ab4d79a7fb13fe93f4d7","html_url":"https://github.com/torvalds/linux/commit/62b13f41be6284250c06ab4d79a7fb13fe93f4d7"},{"sha":"855abf2cf8cd69a248362ca4b518de9387dd6bf5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/torvalds/linux/commits/855abf2cf8cd69a248362ca4b518de9387dd6bf5","html_url":"https://github.com/torvalds/linux/commit/855abf2cf8cd69a248362ca4b518de9387dd6bf5"}]},"merge_base_commit":{"sha":"5258572aa5fd5a7ed01b123b28241e0281b6fb9b","node_id":"C_kwDOACN7MtoAKDUyNTg1NzJhYTVmZDVhN2VkMDFiMTIzYjI4MjQxZTAyODFiNmZiOWI","commit":{"author":{"name":"Nicholas Carlini","email":"nicholas@carlini.com","date":"2026-03-08T23:29:49Z"},"committer":{"name":"Steve French","email":"stfrench@microsoft.com","date":"2026-03-18T02:45:29Z"},"message":"ksmbd: fix share_conf UAF in tree_conn disconnect\n\n__ksmbd_tree_conn_disconnect() drops the share_conf reference before\nchecking tree_conn->refcount. When someone uses SMB3 multichannel and\nbinds two connections to one session, a SESSION_LOGOFF on connection A\ncalls ksmbd_conn_wait_idle(conn) which only drains connection A's\nrequest counter, not connection B's. This means there's a race condition:\nrequests already dispatched on connection B hold tree_conn references via\nwork->tcon. The disconnect path frees share_conf while those requests\nare still walking work->tcon->share_conf, causing a use-after-free.\n\nThis fix combines the share_conf put with the tree_conn free so it\nonly happens when the last reference is dropped.\n\nFixes: b39a1833cc4a (\"ksmbd: fix use-after-free in ksmbd_tree_connect_put under concurrency\")\nSigned-off-by: Nicholas Carlini <nicholas@carlini.com>\nAcked-by: Namjae Jeon <linkinjeon@kernel.org>\nSigned-off-by: Steve French <stfrench@microsoft.com>","tree":{"sha":"0544e60318d4d9f4d6b7e0e5be14921f3c6ff109","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/torvalds/linux/git/trees/0544e60318d4d9f4d6b7e0e5be14921f3c6ff109"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/torvalds/linux/git/commits/5258572aa5fd5a7ed01b123b28241e0281b6fb9b","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":false,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"payload":null,"verified_at":null}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/torvalds/linux/commits/5258572aa5fd5a7ed01b123b28241e0281b6fb9b","html_url":"https://github.com/torvalds/linux/commit/5258572aa5fd5a7ed01b123b28241e0281b6fb9b","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/torvalds/linux/commits/5258572aa5fd5a7ed01b123b28241e0281b6fb9b/comments","author":{"login":"carlini","id":1269300,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEyNjkzMDA=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1269300?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/carlini","html_url":"https://github.com/carlini","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/carlini/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/carlini/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/carlini/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.githu